<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY H1 TRADE GAP $1.145BLN,UP $51MLN VS H1 '96.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY H1 TRADE GAP $1.145BLN,UP $51MLN VS H1 '96.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's foreign trade deficit in the first half was $1.145 billion, up $51 million from the same 1996 period, the Ministry of Industry and Trade said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Exports in the first half rose 15.1 percent to $8.624 billion, and imports jumped 13.8 percent to $9.769 billion from the first six months of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (361) 327 4040</p>
</text>
